{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-ebda225f-c532-4557-8ac0-553672a262d3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-a9d8bf45d0034cc2","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8010-70gyc9k5/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8010-E001.md","content":"# Convert manager binary reconciliation error logs to structured resource context\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic delivers the structured-logging conversion for the rhods-operator manager binary. All reconciliation error logs across the manager's five controller tiers — the DataScienceCluster (DSC) controller, 8 component controllers (DataSciencePipelines, Kueue, ModelRegistry, Ray, SparkOperator, Trainer, TrainingOperator, TrustyAI), the module controller with its 8 module handlers (Dashboard, AIGateway, KServe, OGX, Workbenches, MLflowOperator, FeastOperator, MCPLifecycleOperator), the DSCInitialization (DSCI) controller, and 5 service controllers (Gateway, Auth, Monitoring, CertConfigMapGenerator, Setup) — plus all 12 manager-side action files (8 component + 3 service + 1 DSC + 3 module, minus the cloudmanager-independent set described in Scope) emit resource identity as structured key-value pairs (`name`, `namespace`, `resourceKind`) instead of embedding it in message strings. The DSCI controller's non-standard key names (`Request.Name`, `DSCInitialization`) are migrated to the standard camelCase convention.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Audit all `log.Error()` call sites in reconciliation error paths across the manager binary's controllers and action files, using grep/static analysis to produce a tracked checklist of call sites (confirming the strategy's ~75% embedded-identity estimate).\n- For each call site embedding resource name or namespace in the message string, extract the identity fields and convert to structured key-value pairs (`name`, `namespace`), removing the redundant identity from the message text.\n- Migrate the DSCI controller's structured field names from `Request.Name`/`DSCInitialization` to `name`/`namespace`.\n- Add `resourceKind` as a structured field to all reconciliation error logs: service controllers, module controller (all 8 module handlers), DSCI, and action files where kind is not implied by controller name (P0), and DSC + component controllers for cross-controller queryability (P1, same call sites).\n- Action files in scope: 8 component action files (`components/<name>/<name>_controller_actions.go`), 3 service action files (`services/{auth,gateway,monitoring}/*_controller_actions.go`), 1 DSC action file (`datasciencecluster/datasciencecluster_controller_actions.go`), 3 module action files (`modules/modules_controller_actions*.go`).\n- Handle cluster-scoped resources (e.g., DataScienceCluster, DSCInitialization): emit `name` and `resourceKind`, with `namespace` omitted or set to empty string — no spurious namespace value.\n- Author and verify the CI lint rule (or static-analysis check) covering the manager binary's converted call sites: it flags any `log.Error` call in the manager binary with name/namespace embedded in message text or missing required structured fields.\n- Unit tests asserting field presence and correctness via a test logger for each controller tier and action-file tier.\n- Log consumer regression validation: deploy a test build to a dev cluster with the production log consumer stack configured, trigger sample reconciliation errors, and compare before/after log output — structured fields present, and the log consumer (Loki, CloudWatch) ingests both formats without configuration changes.\n- Coordinate with SRE/Support to identify text-based alert rules that rely on the changed message-string patterns (identification and hand-off only; updating the rules is SRE-owned and out of scope).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given any manager-binary reconciliation error log call that previously embedded resource name or namespace in the message string, when the code is updated, then the call uses structured key-value pairs (`name`, `namespace`), measured by the CI lint rule or static analysis flagging zero remaining `log.Error` calls in the manager binary with name/namespace embedded in message text.\n- Given the DSCI controller's reconciliation error logs, when the code is updated, then all structured field names use the camelCase convention (`name`, `namespace`, `resourceKind`), measured by unit test asserting DSCI error logs contain the standard field names and a codebase grep confirming no references to `Request.Name`/`DSCInitialization` as log keys remain.\n- Given a service controller (Gateway, Auth, Monitoring, CertConfigMapGenerator, Setup) encounters a reconciliation error, when the error is logged, then the entry includes `resourceKind`, measured by unit test parsing test logger output and asserting `resourceKind` is present with the correct value.\n- Given an action-file error log across any of the 4 tiers (8 component, 3 service, 1 DSC, 3 module), when the code is updated, then the entry includes `name`, `namespace`, and `resourceKind`, measured by unit test asserting all three fields are present with correct values across all 15 action files.\n- Given the module controller reconciles any of its 8 module handlers and encounters an error, when the error is logged, then the entry includes `name`, `namespace`, and `resourceKind`, measured by unit test asserting field presence and correctness.\n- Given DSC and component controller reconciliation error logs, when the code is updated, then entries include `resourceKind` for cross-controller queryability, measured by unit test asserting `resourceKind` presence.\n- Given a cluster-scoped resource (e.g., DataScienceCluster, DSCInitialization) is reconciled and encounters an error, when the error is logged, then the entry includes `name` and `resourceKind` with `namespace` omitted or empty, measured by unit test confirming no spurious namespace value.\n- The CI lint rule covering the manager binary's call sites runs in CI and passes on the converted codebase, and fails on a deliberately re-introduced message-embedded identity call.\n- Before/after log output comparison for a sample reconciliation error from a dev-cluster test build confirms structured fields appear and the production log consumer stack ingests both formats without configuration changes.\n- A list of identified text-based alert rules relying on changed message-string patterns is delivered to SRE/Support.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-1 (P0) — conversion of message-embedded name/namespace to structured KV pairs in manager-binary reconciliation error logs (manager portion).\n- HLR-2 (P0) — DSCI controller migrated from `Request.Name`/`DSCInitialization` to camelCase convention.\n- HLR-3 (P0) — service controller error logs include `resourceKind`.\n- HLR-4 (P0) — all action-file error logs include `name`, `namespace`, `resourceKind` across all 4 tiers (8 component + 3 service + 1 DSC + 3 module).\n- HLR-6 (P0) — module controller error logs include `name`, `namespace`, `resourceKind` (8 module handlers).\n- HLR-7 (P1) — DSC and component controller error logs include `resourceKind` (bundled: same `log.Error` call sites as the HLR-1/HLR-4 conversions; adding one key-value pair to lines already being edited — a separate epic would re-audit and re-edit the same files twice).\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":64275,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a580b57804d2fe22","agent_id":"af8a167483ade832b","session_id":"24eb6c29-6a9a-48c1-874c-32ca163b119c","uuid":"672cf159-6f3e-419a-9144-109c70c160aa","timestamp":"2026-10-26T19:40:38.119Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8010"}
